 "traps": [
  "the only manifest is requirements.txt, a full pip freeze of 54 pinned names with no project name: the unit is named by its root and its dependencies have unit null",
  "requirements.txt does not separate direct from transitive packages and no other file does: all 54 lines are declared there with ==, so they are all listed; the code imports only 21 of them (alembic, click, elasticsearch, Flask, flask-babel, Flask-HTTPAuth, Flask-Login, Flask-Mail, Flask-Migrate, Flask-Moment, Flask-SQLAlchemy, Flask-WTF, langdetect, PyJWT, python-dotenv, redis, requests, rq, SQLAlchemy, Werkzeug, WTForms), gunicorn is run by Procfile and boot.sh, and names such as certifi, idna, greenlet or httpie are imported nowhere",
  "there is no lockfile: the == pins are the declared range and resolved stays null",
  "the distribution name differs from the import name: PyJWT is imported as jwt, python-dotenv as dotenv, Flask-HTTPAuth as flask_httpauth, psycopg2-binary would be psycopg2",
  "Dockerfile line 5 installs gunicorn, pymysql and cryptography with pip outside requirements.txt and without a version: pymysql and cryptography are declared by no manifest and are not in dependencies; MySQL is a service only because of that line",
  "no file declares a Python version: Dockerfile says FROM python:slim, a tag without a version, and there is no runtime.txt, .python-version, pyproject.toml or CI workflow; Vagrantfile names the box ubuntu/jammy64, an operating system and not a toolchain",
  "the database is whatever DATABASE_URL names: config.py falls back to the SQLite file app.db and rewrites postgres:// to postgresql://; psycopg2-binary is in requirements.txt and never imported, pymysql comes only from the Dockerfile",
  "Redis is the RQ queue microblog-tasks, not a cache; Elasticsearch is optional (app.elasticsearch is None without ELASTICSEARCH_URL) and mail goes to whatever SMTP server MAIL_SERVER names",
  "one unit, three ways in: the web app microblog.py (FLASK_APP in .flaskenv, gunicorn microblog:app in Procfile, boot.sh and the supervisor file), the RQ worker that imports app/tasks.py by the dotted name app.tasks.export_posts built as a string in app/models.py, and tests.py run directly with unittest",
  "config.py is a top-level module next to the app package (from config import Config), not part of it",
  "app/templates/*.html and the two .txt mail templates are Jinja2 under plain extensions; migrations/script.py.mako is a Mako template, not Python; deployment/nginx/microblog is an nginx configuration with no extension",
  "Bootstrap 5.3.2 is loaded from the jsDelivr CDN in app/templates/base.html and Moment.js is injected by Flask-Moment: neither is a dependency in any manifest",
  "migrations/versions/*.py were autogenerated by Alembic and then kept and edited in the repository: they are project code, not excluded; migrations/alembic.ini, env.py and script.py.mako come from the Flask-Migrate template",
  "app/translations/es/LC_MESSAGES/messages.po is the hand-translated Spanish catalog and is kept; the compiled .mo files are ignored by .gitignore and exist only after flask translate compile, which the Dockerfile and the Procfile run",
  "app/cli.py shells out to pybabel with os.system: the commands are strings, not imports",
  "deployment/ holds an nginx site and two supervisor programs written for /home/ubuntu/microblog: they describe one deployment and are not needed to run the app",
  "config.py loads an .env file that is not in the repository",
  "the Microsoft Translator endpoint and the Gravatar URL are written in the code (app/translate.py, app/models.py); only the translator key comes from the environment"
 ],
